{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int N = 300010;\nint n, K, mod;\nint dp[N][20];\nint cnt[N], mx[N];\nint fact[N], invFact[N];\n\nint power(int x, int y) {\n    int res = 1;\n    while (y) {\n        if (y & 1) res = (long long)res * x % mod;\n        x = (long long)x * x % mod;\n        y >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint C(int i, int j) {\n    return (long long)fact[i] * invFact[j] % mod * invFact[i - j] % mod;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d%d%d\", &n, &K, &mod);\n    if (n & 1) {\n        printf(\"%d\\n\", power(K, n));\n        return 0;\n    }\n    fact[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) fact[i] = (long long)fact[i - 1] * i % mod;\n    invFact[n] = power(fact[n], mod - 2);\n    invFact[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 1; --i) invFact[i] = (long long)invFact[i + 1] * (i + 1) % mod;\n    // Compute cnt and mx without builtins\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        int x = i;\n        int pop = 0;\n        int high = 0;\n        for (int b = 0; b < 20; ++b) {\n            if (x & (1 << b)) {\n                pop++;\n                high = 1 << b;\n            }\n        }\n        cnt[i] = pop;\n        mx[i] = high;\n    }\n    dp[0][0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        if ((n & i) != i) continue;\n        int now = i ^ mx[i];\n        // iterate submasks using for loop with decrement\n        for (int k = now; ; k = (k - 1) & now) {\n            int cur1 = k + mx[i];\n            int cur2 = i ^ cur1;\n            int up = min(K - 1, cnt[cur2]);\n            int tmp = C(i, cur1);\n            for (int j = 0; j <= up; ++j) {\n                dp[i][j + 1] = (dp[i][j + 1] + (long long)dp[cur2][j] * tmp) % mod;\n            }\n            if (k == 0) break;\n        }\n    }\n    int ans = 0;\n    int lim = min(cnt[n], K);\n    for (int j = 1; j <= lim; ++j) {\n        ans = (ans + (long long)dp[n][j] * C(K, j) % mod * fact[j]) % mod;\n    }\n    ans = (power(K, n) - ans + mod) % mod;\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", ans);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    K = int(data[1])\n    mod = int(data[2])\n\n    if n & 1:\n        print(pow(K, n, mod))\n        return\n\n    # precompute factorials and inverse factorials up to n\n    fact = [1] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        fact[i] = fact[i-1] * i % mod\n    inv_fact = [1] * (n + 1)\n    inv_fact[n] = pow(fact[n], mod - 2, mod)\n    for i in range(n, 0, -1):\n        inv_fact[i-1] = inv_fact[i] * i % mod\n\n    # precompute popcount and highest bit for numbers 1..n\n    cnt = [0] * (n + 1)\n    mx = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # popcount\n        pop = 0\n        x = i\n        while x:\n            pop += x & 1\n            x >>= 1\n        cnt[i] = pop\n        # highest bit\n        high = 1 << (i.bit_length() - 1)\n        mx[i] = high\n\n    # dp[i][j] for j up to 19 (since cnt[i] <= 19 for i <= 300000)\n    dp = [[0] * 20 for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # helper for binomial coefficient\n    def C(nn, kk):\n        if kk < 0 or kk > nn:\n            return 0\n        return fact[nn] * inv_fact[kk] % mod * inv_fact[nn - kk] % mod\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if (n & i) != i:\n            continue\n        now = i ^ mx[i]\n        k = now\n        while True:\n            cur1 = k + mx[i]\n            cur2 = i ^ cur1\n            up = min(K - 1, cnt[cur2])\n            tmp = C(i, cur1)\n            for j in range(up + 1):\n                dp[i][j + 1] = (dp[i][j + 1] + dp[cur2][j] * tmp) % mod\n            if k == 0:\n                break\n            k = (k - 1) & now\n\n    ans = 0\n    lim = min(cnt[n], K)\n    for j in range(1, lim + 1):\n        ans = (ans + dp[n][j] * C(K, j) % mod * fact[j]) % mod\n    ans = (pow(K, n, mod) - ans + mod) % mod\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.172316494077677e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00012575789878610522, -2.539125671319198e-05, 0.0, -0.00020454221521504223, -0.00018142008048016578, -0.39441540837287903, -0.02975122630596161, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.3232143828645349e-05, 0.0, -0.02975388802587986, 0.0, -0.0011803095694631338, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.029750648885965347, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -2.753696753643453e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.018157687038183212, -0.5759682059288025, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0380532331764698, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -7.152301259338856e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -6.7949063122